    },
    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 558,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Molecular characterization of the yeast meiotic regulatory gene RIM1.\nWe have used the cloned RIM1 gene to create a complete rim1 deletion. This null allele, like previously isolated rim1 mutations, causes a partial meiotic defect. In addition to RIM1, maximum IME1 expression requires the MCK1 and IME4 gene products. Defects associated with rim1, mck1, and ime4 mutations in expression of a meiotic reporter gene (ime2-lacZ) and in sporulation are additive. These findings suggest that RIM1 acts independently of MCK1 and IME4 to stimulate IME1 expression."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
